{# Where one value in the conflicts panel was read from.

   The file name first, because that is what the lawyer has open next to the
   screen. The kind of document and the id are the fallback: a value whose source
   cannot be named is one they would have to re-derive from the pile by hand.
   No confidence figure: it is the extractor's own estimate of how clearly it
   read the text, not which document is right, and read as a percentage it
   points the lawyer at the wrong question. #}
{% set name = option.documentId is not null ? document_names[option.documentId]|default(null) : null %}
{% if name %}<span class="font-medium">{{ name }}</span>{% endif %}
{% if option.documentType is not null %}{% if name %} · {% endif %}{{ option.documentType.label|trans }}{% elseif not name %}{{ 'wizard.conflict.unknown_document'|trans }}{% endif %}
{% if option.documentId is not null and not name %} #{{ option.documentId }}{% endif %}
